## Task 1: Identifying Recursion

Yes, the sentence contains **prepositional phrase recursion (PP recursion)**. The PP *"in a glass of whiskey"* contains a smaller PP *"of whiskey"* nested inside it. Formally:

$$PP_1 \rightarrow P' \rightarrow P + NP$$
$$NP \rightarrow N' \rightarrow N + PP_2$$
$$PP_2 \rightarrow P' \rightarrow P + NP$$

So we have:

> **[PP in [NP a glass [PP of whiskey]]]**

A PP dominates an NP which dominates another PP — this is the hallmark of **embedded/nested PP recursion**.

